### MIT packages (representative)

- `packages/envsync-kernel`
- `packages/envsync-api` (core product surface)
- `packages/deploy`, `packages/deploy-core`
- `apps/envsync-web` (dashboard shell)
- `apps/envsync-landing`
- Public SDKs under `sdks/` that are not management/enterprise-only

## 2. Proprietary — EnvSync Enterprise License

The following paths are **not** MIT. They are proprietary software. Production
use requires a valid EnvSync enterprise subscription or other written license
from EnvSync Cloud. See the LICENSE file inside each package for terms:

| Path | Package |
|------|---------|
| `packages/envsync-enterprise/` | Management module registry + EE API surface |
| `packages/envsync-enterprise-web/` | Enterprise dashboard modules |
| _(retired)_ `packages/envsync-management-api/` | Removed — manage is `/api/v1/manage` on core API |
| _(retired)_ `sdks/envsync-management-*-sdk/` | Removed — use core `envsync-ts-sdk` / `envsync-go-sdk` |
| `packages/deploy-cli/` | Published as `@envsync-cloud/deploy-enterprise` |

Enterprise source may appear in this **public monorepo** for transparency and
contribution workflow. That does **not** grant a production enterprise license.
Signing keys for entitlements live only on EnvSync’s private license-server.

## 3. Contributions

- Contributions to MIT paths are accepted under the MIT License.
- Contributions to proprietary paths are accepted under terms that allow EnvSync
  Cloud to include them under the EnvSync Enterprise License (see CONTRIBUTING.md).

## 4. Product editions (non-legal summary)

| Product | License | Notes |
|---------|---------|--------|
| Hosted EnvSync Cloud | Commercial SaaS | Platform-operated |
| Self-host OSS | MIT | Single-org; public deploy CLI |
| Self-host Enterprise | Proprietary + subscription | Verified entitlements; management process |

See `EDITIONING.md` and `docs/SUPPORT.md` for the full support matrix.
